    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/project-assistant/1209/100654308400": {
      "title": "Project Assistant",
      "description": "Project Assistant at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Project Assistant Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20178938 Category Administrative Support Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Department of Population and Public Health Sciences is in search of a dependable, flexible, and detail-oriented individual is needed to join a research team at the University of Southern California to participate in interventional studies using high-efficiency particulate air (HEPA) filtration to potentially help with cardiometabolic health. Employment involves (1) contacting potential participants for interest and willingness to participate in the study using electronic medical records; (2) coordinating home visit time with participants and maintain the contact with participants during follow-up; (3) conducting interviews in English or Spanish; (4) setting up air purifiers and air pollution monitors at residential houses, (5) transporting biospecimen and managing sample shipment for laboratory analysis; (6) using REDCap system to track recruitment and follow-up and enter data into databases; (7) preparing study documents including IRB applications and progress reports and providing project support to the research study and the study staff personnel and faculty investigators; and (8) assist managing Redcap database, sample manifest, and statistical analysis.  Excellent English writing, speaking and communication skills are required . Bilingual (English/Spanish) is preferred. Prior experience in a research environment and participants recruitment and follow-up is required. Experience with statistical analysis and interventional studies is preferred. The candidate needs to have strong organizational capabilities, superb problem-solving skills, and a demonstrated ability to work independently while managing multiple tasks. Flexible working hours including evenings and weekends may be needed. Knowledge of REDCap database development and management will be highly preferred. Bachelor’s degree in a public health related field is preferred. Licensed phlebotomist is preferred but not required. The hourly rate range for this position is $25.96. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations Minimum Education: High school or equivalent\nMinimum Experience: 1 year\nMinimum Field of Expertise: Knowledge of data collection procedures and some experience with proposal preparation and production of technical documents Job ID REQ20178938 Posted Date 09/15/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Mission USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Postdoctoral Scholar Research Associate Los Angeles, California Save Job RN Clinical, Lead - Infusion Center - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job LVN I - Torrance-BCO Ortho Clinic- Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Torrance, California Save Job Scheduler - LV Durango Family Med Cl - Full Time 10 Hour Rotating Shifts (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Las Vegas, Nevada No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Al