    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/postdoctoral-scholar-research-associate/1209/99181493904": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar Research Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar Research Associate at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Postdoctoral Scholar Research Associate Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20178885 Category Postdoctoral Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Dr. Beiyun Zhou’s lab is recruiting a Postdoctoral/ Research Associate. Dr. Zhou’s lab is interested in studying the cell and molecular biology of the alveolar epithelium with focus on analysis of alveolar epithelial cell (AEC) differentiation and plasticity in the context of lung injury and fibrosis. The position is for qualified candidates who wish to pursue a career in the basic and translational research of lung disease idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF). Responsibilities and Duties Plans, designs, and conducts highly technical and complex research projects independently. Conducts cellular and molecular experiments for hypothesis-driven research Analyzes, interprets, summarizes and compiles data Present research data at lab meetings, scientific conferences, and in peer-reviewed publications under the direction of the Principal Investigator Contribute to the preparation of grant applications, progress reports, and manuscripts. Stay current with developments in the field and contribute innovative ideas to advance the research program Be responsible for teaching techniques to other lab members Serves as a project liaison between the lab and its collaborators Maintain accurate research records and ensure compliance with institutional, funding agency, and laboratory safety policies Performs other related duties as assigned or requested. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in biomedical sciences or related disciplines . Previous training and experiences in the following research areas are preferred: 1) experience in molecular biology, biochemistry, and pathology; 2) mechanistic studies of metabolic pathways and mitochondrial function; 3) mechanistic studies of lung fibrosis; 4) experience in working with mouse models ; 5) experience in bioinformatics such as ScRNAseq and ChIP-seq. Minimum education: Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate within the previous three years. Salary Range: The annual base salary range for this position is $70,304. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations.“ Minimum Education: Ph.D.\n\nPreferred: Ph.D. in biomedical sciences or related disciplines Job ID REQ20178885 Posted Date 08/13/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More 八月 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More 七月 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More 七月 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Mission USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More 七月 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More 八月 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More 九月 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More 二月 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More 六月 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More 七月 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Postdoctoral Scholar Research Associate Los Angeles, California Save Job RN Clinical, Lead - Infusion Center - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job LVN I - Torrance-BCO Ortho Clinic- Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Torrance, California Save Job Scheduler - LV Durango Family Med Cl - Full Time 10 Hour Rotating Shifts (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Las Vegas, Nevada No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re 