    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/big-ten-fellow/1209/100703333760": {
      "title": "Big Ten Fellow",
      "description": "Big Ten Fellow at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Big Ten Fellow Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180971 Category Administrative Support Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Big Ten Fellow The University of Southern California (USC) is one of the world’s leading private research universities. An anchor institution in Los Angeles and a global center for arts, technology, and international business, USC is also one of the largest private employers in the City of Los Angeles. We are searching for exceptional individuals to help us fulfill our mission: developing individuals and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. As an employee of USC, you will be part of a world-class research university and a member of the “Trojan Family,” which is comprised of the faculty, students, and staff who make the university what it is. USC Athletics aims to inspire champions in competition and in the classroom. We exist to enrich the lives of students to positively impact our community and world for generations to come. Operating with the four core values of Competitive Spirit, Togetherness, Passionate Pride for USC, and Our Courage to Blaze the Trail, the Trojans choose to lead by example. With more than 600 student-athletes competing across USC’s 23 sports programs, USC Athletics is committed to serving as an unmatched destination for talented student-athletes to reach their fullest potential in all that they do, while offering them the opportunity to compete for NCAA and Big Ten championships and work toward a degree from one of the world’s leading universities. USC Athletics is seeking a Big Ten Fellow to join its community of staff members and student-athletes. USC Athletics’ Big Ten Fellowship provides an entry-level opportunity to gain hands-on administrative experience within a Big Ten athletics department. The program is designed to expand access to careers in intercollegiate athletics while supporting participants’ professional development, leadership skills, and career goals. Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Student-Athlete Development, the Big Ten Fellow Intern will collaborate with the Student-Athlete Development team and other areas within USC Athletics. The Fellow will assist with day-to-day departmental operations and programs that support the personal and professional development, career preparation, and skill development of USC student-athletes. The fellowship provides hands-on experience in athletics administration, with a primary focus on student-athlete development programming and exposure to various functions of a collegiate athletics department. Knowledge of or experience working in higher education or intercollegiate athletics is preferred. An understanding of the unique culture and needs of Division I student-athletes is also preferred. This position serves a large student and staff population, must demonstrate a commitment to improving outcomes for a variety of populations, and is expected to contribute to the program’s demonstrated commitment to non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all. This is a non-exempt position with work expected to be performed in person. Roles and Responsibilities · Creates and manages content across social media platforms, including Instagram, X/Twitter, LinkedIn, YouTube, and emerging platforms, to support Athletics’ digital presence. · Captures and edits photo and video content using mobile and other available technology for use across departmental channels. · Collects, analyzes, and summarizes data for formative and summative reporting, including developing surveys and forms using tools such as Google Forms. · Designs graphics and edits video content using tools such as Canva Pro to support marketing, communications, and promotional materials. · Monitors departmental email correspondence and prepares documents, reports, presentations, and other materials using Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and related applications. · Participates in the development, implementation, and execution of projects, programs, events, and committees that advance student-athlete development initiatives. · Researches and recommends strategies related to best practices, emerging trends, and policy considerations affecting student-athlete development initiatives. · Collaborates with Athletics colleagues and campus partners on events, programs, and initiatives that support Trojan Athletics and programming for student-athletes and employees. · Assists with the execution of the Trojan Student-Athlete Development Unit Operating Plan and preparation of the unit’s year-end report. · Develops professional relationships and engages, as appropriate, with the NCAA, Big Ten Conference, campus partners, and other professional organizations in support of student-athlete development goals and initiatives. · Assists with additional projects and administrative responsibilities that provide exposure to the operations and functions of an intercollegiate athletics department. · Performs other related duties as assigned or requested. The University reserves the right to add or change duties at any time. Minimum Qualifications · Bachelor’s degree. · Excellent oral and written communication skills. · Ability to work effectively and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. · Proficiency with word-processing, spreadsheet, presentation, and email applications. · Ability to collect, organize, analyze, and summarize data and develop surveys and forms. · Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. · Ability to manage multiple assignments, priorities, and deadlines. · Ability to collaborate effectively with student-athletes, coaches, staff, administrators, campus partners, and external organizations. · Experience working in higher education, intercollegiate athletics, student-athlete development, or a related environment. · Knowledge of collegiate athletics and the unique culture and developmental needs of Division I student-athletes. · Experience developing digital or social media content. · Experience with graphic-design and video-editing tools such as Canva Pro. · Experience creating surveys, collecting data, and preparing reports or presentations. · Demonstrated interest in pursuing or further developing a career in intercollegiate athletics administration. Driving Requirement A valid driver’s license and participation in the University’s Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV) Pull Notice System may be required if driving is an assigned responsibility of the position. If required, a satisfactory DMV record will be a final condition of employment in accordance with applicable University policy. USC Unifying Values In addition, the successful candidate must demonstrate, through ideas, words, and actions, a strong commitment to USC’s Unifying Values. Compensation The hourly rate for this position is $25.00 per hour . When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as, but not limited to, the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education and training, key skills, internal peer alignment, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. To Apply All candidates must submit a resume with their application. Additional materials may be requested at a later date. All USC employees will undergo reference checking and background screening prior to hire in accordance with applicable University policies and legal requirements. Equal Opportunity and Reasonable Accommodation USC is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration. Minimum Qualifications\n•Bachelor’s degree.\n•Excellent oral and written communication skills.\n•Ability to work effectively and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment.\n•Proficiency with word-processing, spreadsheet, presentation, and email applications.\n•Ability to collect, organize, analyze, and summarize data and develop surveys and forms.\n•Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.\n•Ability to manage multiple assignments, priorities, and deadlines.\n•Ability to collaborate effectively with student-athletes, coaches, staff, administrators, campus partners, and external organizations.\n•Experience working in higher education, intercollegiate athletics, student-athlete development, or a related environment.\n•Knowledge of collegiate athletics and the unique culture and developmental needs of Division I student-athletes.\n•Experience developing digital or social media content.\n•Experience with graphic-design and video-editing tools such as Canva Pro.\n•Experience creating surveys, collecting data, and preparing reports or presentations.\n•Demonstrated interest in pursuing or further developing a career in intercollegiate athletics administration. Job ID REQ20180971 Posted Date 09/16/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Adjunct Instructor of Local Governance Los Angeles, California Save Job Protocol Coordinator (RN) Los Angeles, California Save Job RN Supervisor (Cardiovascular) - Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job RN Staff - 7 N Tele - Full Time 12 Hour Nights (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, Cal