    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/project-assistant/1209/100684986848": {
      "title": "Project Assistant",
      "description": "Project Assistant at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Project Assistant Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180662 Category Administrative Support Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is located in the heart of downtown Los Angeles and is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. USC is consistently ranked among the nation’s most prestigious universities, and the USC Leonard Davis School of Gerontology features one of the world’s best degree and research programs in gerontology. The USC Leonard Davis School of Gerontology has an international reputation as a hub of aging research and with additional strong programs throughout the university, leads the way in defining and advancing the field of gerontology: https://gero.usc.edu The Lee Lab at the USC Leonard Davis School of Gerontology is seeking a Project Assistant (fixed-term, 4 months) to join our staff and student community. Our lab studies mitochondria-derived peptides (MDPs), a class of small bioactive peptides encoded in the mitochondrial genome, including MOTS-c. We investigate how these peptides regulate metabolism, cellular stress responses, and aging, and how they can be developed into therapeutics for age-related diseases, including cancer. This is a hands-on bench position that functions as the lab's core staff scientist and lab manager. The Project Assistant (Fixed-Term)will run experiments end to end, keep the lab running day to day, and contribute to manuscripts and grant applications. The work includes mammalian cell culture, mouse studies (handling, treatment and dosing, metabolic phenotyping, tissue collection), molecular and biochemical assays, live-cell imaging, sample processing, and data entry and management. Reporting directly to the Principal Investigator, Dr. Changhan David Lee, the Project Assistant will work closely with the lab's graduate students and postdocs as well as collaborators across USC, including the Keck School of Medicine and the Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center. The ideal candidate will have hands-on experience with cell culture and standard molecular biology techniques, working familiarity with Microsoft Office and common data analysis and imaging software (e.g., GraphPad Prism, ImageJ), excellent communication skills, and strong attention to detail. Previous experience as a Research Assistant or technician in a molecular biology, cell biology, biochemistry, or physiology lab is preferred; mouse handling experience is a plus. This position requires careful record keeping, sound judgment in a shared lab environment, and the ability to work independently and as part of a team. Roles and responsibilities include: Under the direction of the PI, perform and assist with experiments, including cell culture, mouse studies, tissue and sample collection and processing, molecular and biochemical assays (e.g., western blotting, qPCR, ELISA, immunostaining and microscopy, metabolic assays), basic data analysis, and record keeping. General lab management: maintaining and ordering supplies and reagents, equipment maintenance, and maintaining compliance with safety, training, and animal-use protocols (IACUC, IBC, EH&S), including protocol amendments and renewals. Performing literature reviews, grant submissions, publications, figure and methods preparation, and reports. Training and supporting new lab members, including undergraduate and rotation students. Performs other related duties as assigned or requested. The University reserves the right to add or change duties at any time. Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate will possess a bachelor's degree in biology, biochemistry, molecular or cell biology, physiology, neuroscience, or a related science field. Combined experience/education as a substitute for minimum education. Hands-on laboratory experience with cell culture and molecular biology techniques; prior mouse work is strongly preferred. Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills are essential. The candidate must have the ability to work independently and have a passion for the lab's scientific mission and a commitment to exceptional quality. This is a non-exempt position with work expected on campus and occasionally on weekends (e.g., for animal studies and time-course experiments). Benefits include a competitive salary and a rich array of USC benefits including healthcare (including dental and vision), 403(b), tuition reimbursement, national holidays, paid vacation, and more. The hourly rate range for this position is $25.96-$29.19. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. This position is funded by a research grant. Accordingly, your position is contingent upon receipt of the necessary funding from this grant to continue employment. If you are interested, please submit your completed application, including a cover letter and resume with references. Thank you for your interest! Minimum Education: High school or equivalent\nMinimum Experience: 1 year\nMinimum Field of Expertise: Knowledge of data collection procedures and some experience with proposal preparation and production of technical documents Job ID REQ20180662 Posted Date 09/15/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Adjunct Instructor of Local Governance Los Angeles, California Save Job Protocol Coordinator (RN) Los Angeles, California Save Job RN Supervisor (Cardiovascular) - Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job RN Staff - 7 N Tele - Full Time 12 Hour Nights (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from the list of options. Finally, click \"Add\" to create your job alert. Job Category Select a Job Category Academic Advising Academic Advising and Career Counseling Accounting, Finance and Banking Administration Administrative Support Athletics Auxiliary Services Biomedical Business and Financial Management Child Care Services Clinical Administration Compliance Data Analysis Dentistry Development and Fundraising Facilities Management Facilities Management and Construction Faculty Faculty and Teaching Faculty Development Genetics Grants Administration & Sponsored Programs Health and Medical Services Human Resources Information Technology Information Technology Services Institutional Research and Planning Keck Medicine of USC Laboratory Laboratory and Research Legal Services Libraries Marketing and Events Multimedia Nursing Nursing Services Pharmacy Physician Assistant Postdoctoral Public Safety Research and Clinical Support Research and Grants Administration Social Work